No search needed — this is pure wiring. Let me show exactly where `RoutingQueryBuilder` sits in the call chain, with all the pieces connected end-to-end.

## The call chain at a glance

```
ChatController
   └─► ChatService.chatStream(sessionId, userMessage)
          ├─► 1. RoutingService.decide(sessionId, userMessage)
          │        ├─► RoutingQueryBuilder.build(sessionId, userMessage)   ← builds the ROUTING query
          │        ├─► SemanticIntentRouter.route(routingQuery)            ← vector search
          │        └─► SessionIntentCache (sticky fallback)
          └─► 2. chatClient.prompt().user(userMessage) ...                 ← ORIGINAL message to LLM
                       .tools(scopedTools)                                 ← scoped by the decision
```

Key rule to keep in mind while wiring: **`RoutingQueryBuilder`'s output is used only for the vector search — never sent to the LLM and never stored in memory.**

## 1. The beans you need (recap + one new one)

You already have `RoutingQueryBuilder`, `SemanticIntentRouter`, and `SessionIntentCache` from the previous answer. Add Caffeine for the cache if you haven't:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.github.ben-manes.caffeine</groupId>
    <artifactId>caffeine</artifactId>
