```

Now compose them into one **`RoutingService`** so `ChatService` stays clean:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class RoutingService {

    private final RoutingQueryBuilder queryBuilder;
    private final SemanticIntentRouter router;
    private final SessionIntentCache intentCache;

    private static final double STICKY_FALLBACK_THRESHOLD = 0.70;

    public RoutingDecision decide(String sessionId, String userMessage) {

        // Step 1: build the context-enriched routing query
        String routingQuery = queryBuilder.build(sessionId, userMessage);
        log.debug("session={} routingQuery='{}'", sessionId, routingQuery);

        // Step 2: semantic routing on the enriched query
        RoutingDecision decision = router.route(routingQuery);

        // Step 3: sticky-intent fallback for ambiguous follow-ups
        if (decision.unknown() || decision.confidence() < STICKY_FALLBACK_THRESHOLD) {
            Optional<String> sticky = intentCache.lastIntent(sessionId);
            if (sticky.isPresent()) {
                log.info("session={} sticky fallback: {} (score was {})",
                         sessionId, sticky.get(), decision.confidence());
                decision = new RoutingDecision(sticky.get(), 0.0, false);
            }
        }

        // Step 4: remember confident decisions for future follow-ups
        if (!decision.unknown()) {
            intentCache.remember(sessionId, decision.intent(), decision.confidence());
        }

        log.info("session={} intent={} confidence={}",
                 sessionId, decision.intent(), decision.confidence());
        return decision;
    }
}
```

## 2. `RoutingQueryBuilder` — one correction for real-world wiring

One subtle but important detail about how it reads memory. The `MessageChatMemoryAdvisor` **appends the current exchange to memory only after the response completes**. So when `RoutingQueryBuilder.build()` runs (before the LLM call), `chatMemory.get(sessionId)` contains only *previous* turns — which is exactly what you want: the last `USER` message in memory is the *previous* user message, not the current one. No off-by-one filtering needed. ✅

Here's the final version with that assumption made explicit:

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class RoutingQueryBuilder {

    private final ChatMemory chatMemory;

    private static final int SHORT_MESSAGE_THRESHOLD = 20;
    private static final Set<String> CONTINUATION_PREFIXES = Set.of(
            "و ", "بعد", "همچنین", "اون", "آن", "همون", "همان",
            "چطور", "پس ", "خب ", "اگه", "اگر", "چی ", "کی ", "چرا");

    /**
     * Builds the query used ONLY for semantic intent routing.
     * NOTE: must be called BEFORE the ChatClient call — memory then contains
     * only previous turns, so the last USER message is the previous question.
     */
    public String build(String sessionId, String userMessage) {
        String normalized = PersianTextUtils.normalize(userMessage.trim());

        if (!isLikelyFollowUp(normalized)) {
            return normalized;
        }

        return lastUserMessage(sessionId)
                .map(prev -> prev + " — " + normalized)
                .orElse(normalized);
    }

    private Optional<String> lastUserMessage(String sessionId) {
        List<Message> history = chatMemory.get(sessionId);
        if (history == null || history.isEmpty()) return Optional.empty();

        for (int i = history.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {          // walk backwards
            Message m = history.get(i);
            if (m.getMessageType() == MessageType.USER
                    && m.getText() != null && !m.getText().isBlank()) {
                return Optional.of(PersianTextUtils.normalize(m.getText()));
            }
        }
        return Optional.empty();
    }

    private boolean isLikelyFollowUp(String msg) {
        if (msg.length() < SHORT_MESSAGE_THRESHOLD) return true;
        return CONTINUATION_PREFIXES.stream().anyMatch(msg::startsWith);
    }
}
```

(It injects the same `ChatMemory` bean you defined in `ChatConfig` — the JDBC-backed `MessageWindowChatMemory`. Nothing new to configure.)

## 3. The updated `ChatService` — where it all comes together

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class ChatService {

    private final ChatClient chatClient;          // built WITHOUT defaultTools
    private final RoutingService routingService;
    private final List<ChatbotTools> allTools;

    public Flux<ServerSentEvent<String>> chatStream(String sessionId, String userMessage) {

        // ---- ROUTING PHASE (deterministic, ~20-50ms) ----
        RoutingDecision decision = routingService.decide(sessionId, userMessage);

        Object[] scopedTools = decision.unknown()
                ? allTools.toArray()                                   // safety net: all tools
                : allTools.stream()
                          .filter(t -> t.intent().equals(decision.intent()))
                          .toArray();

        // ---- LLM PHASE (original message, scoped tools, full memory) ----
        return chatClient.prompt()
                .user(userMessage)                 // ⚠️ ORIGINAL message — not the routing query
                .advisors(a -> a.param(ChatMemory.CONVERSATION_ID, sessionId))
                .tools(scopedTools)
                .stream()
                .content()
                .map(chunk -> ServerSentEvent.<String>builder()
                        .event("token").data(chunk).build())
                .onErrorResume(ex -> {
                    log.error("Streaming failed session={}", sessionId, ex);
                    return Flux.just(ServerSentEvent.<String>builder()
                            .event("token")
                            .data("متأسفانه خطایی رخ داد. لطفاً دوباره تلاش کنید.")
                            .build());
                });
    }
}
```

And make sure `ChatConfig` no longer registers tools globally (they're now per-request):

```java
@Bean
public ChatClient chatClient(ChatClient.Builder builder, ChatMemory chatMemory) {
    return builder
            .defaultSystem(SYSTEM_PROMPT + "\n" + PROFILE_EXTRACTION_RULES)
            .defaultAdvisors(MessageChatMemoryAdvisor.builder(chatMemory).build())
            // no .defaultTools(...) anymore — ChatService supplies them per request
            .build();
}
```

